::class & object::
What is the primary purpose of using classes and objects? 
{
~ To implement procedural programming 
= To create reusable code through encapsulation 
~ To directly manipulate variables 
~ For low-level memory management
}

::class & object::
What is the difference between a class and an instance of a class? 
{
~ An instance is a member function of a class 
~ They are the same thing 
= A class is a blueprint, an instance is an object created from that class 
~ An instance is the memory allocation for a class
}

::class & object ::
You can define instance attributes outside of the __init__ constructor method.
{
= True
~ False
}

::class & object ::
What is the purpose of the self parameter in Python class methods? 
{
~ It is a keyword to define a class method 
~ It is used for inheritance 
~ It has no specific purpose
= It refers to the current instance of the class
}